{"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec\/reconcile(_:with:in:)-1wwve","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec\/reconcile(_:with:in:)-5oivn"],"title":"Type Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/swiduxrelationcodec"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Enumeration","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxRelationCodec","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"enum","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxRelationCodec","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence0A13RelationCodecO","role":"symbol","title":"SwiduxRelationCodec"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Reconciles a generated model’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relation"},{"text":" properties against the domain","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value being written. Not meant to be called directly.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxRelationCodec"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Why a converter can’t just rebuild its children","level":2,"anchor":"Why-a-converter-cant-just-rebuild-its-children","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The obvious ","type":"text"},{"code":"update(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" body — ","type":"text"},{"code":"self.chapters = try domain.chapters.map { try ChapterModel(from: $0) }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — is a row leak. A relationship’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"deleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fires when the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"parent"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is deleted, never when a child is dropped from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relationship, so the previously-related rows are detached rather than","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"removed: they stay in the store with no owner, and nothing ever collects"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them. Every save of the parent leaves another full copy of its children"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"behind, the store grows for the life of the app, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"toDomain()"},{"type":"text","text":" — which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only walks the current relationship — shows nothing wrong."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So the write-back reconciles by "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead: rows whose identity survives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are updated in place, new identities are inserted, and identities that are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gone are deleted outright."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Identity, not row identity","anchor":"Identity-not-row-identity","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reconciling in place also keeps "},{"code":"persistentModelID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" stable across a save."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That matters beyond tidiness: a rebuilt child is a delete plus an insert, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under CloudKit mirroring every parent edit re-uploads its whole subtree, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every one of those writes a history transaction that a remote-change tick"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then has to resolve."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Duplicates are kept, as everywhere else","anchor":"Duplicates-are-kept-as-everywhere-else","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"text":" emits no ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Attribute(.unique)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (CloudKit forbids unique"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constraints), so several related rows may legitimately share one identity."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are all updated and all kept, matching "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": converging every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matching row is safe, while picking one survivor is not — two devices pick"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"different rows, each tombstones the other’s, and both are lost."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"SwiduxPersistence","abstract":[],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityDB","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityDB","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ModelActor"},{"type":"